From 9843a506386bf473a4a98c752fed0d9553484c81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:37:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] libcameraservice: Fix API1 build breaks from newer
 AudioRestriction/HAL1 base

Several porting gaps surfaced once the build reached this far:

- CameraClient::setAudioRestriction/getGlobalAudioRestriction still used
  the old plain int/int32_t signatures from an older ICamera.h, while the
  interface they override (and the sibling Camera2Client) now use the
  AIDL-backed ICameraDeviceUser::AudioRestriction enum. The parameter-type
  mismatch silently created a non-overriding overload instead of a hard
  error, leaving the pure virtual unimplemented and making CameraClient
  abstract (the actual compile error, at its instantiation site in
  CameraService::connectLegacy).
- That connectLegacy() also had two genuinely dead locals (clientUid/
  clientPid) left over after connectHelper() was changed to take
  clientAttribution directly; -Werror=unused-variable now catches them.
- CameraClient::disconnect() still called the 3-argument
  CameraServiceProxyWrapper::logClose(), which gained an errorState
  parameter; pass 0, matching CameraClient's existing "no device-error
  tracking" behavior (it already always passed deviceError=false).
- HidlProviderInfo.h's HidlDeviceInfo1 (HAL1 provider device info) never
  implemented DeviceInfo's warmUp(), unlike its HidlDeviceInfo3 sibling
  right below it, leaving it abstract too. Add the same
  "not implemented" stub.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ie85c04662e9b81435fb84323d7fe06ab36aa897a
---
 services/camera/libcameraservice/CameraService.cpp     |  3 ---
